   547	        at 18:50:55 and then never logged again — no retry, no error, nothing — while its
   548	        HTTP endpoint kept answering and serving zero tools. The cause is the teardown, not
   549	        the loop: leaving `async with stdio_client(...)` waits for the child to exit, and a
   550	        wedged mcpbridge never does, so the task blocks inside __aexit__ where no `except`
   551	        and no retry can reach it. Every health signal this daemon has says "fine" in that
   552	        state, which is the worst possible failure shape.
   553	
