   555	        a supervisor: launchd, with KeepAlive true. So when an upstream has made no progress
   556	        for STALL_EXIT_SECONDS — no connect attempt, no successful heartbeat — say so loudly
   557	        and exit non-zero. That is the file's own stated philosophy: "a genuine crash is what
   558	        the process supervisor is for." A restart costs one new Xcode approval prompt, which
   559	        the clicker answers.
