   732	        # during an Xcode reconnect Drew's tools, which need no Xcode, vanished too).
   733	        # A connected upstream answering with zero tools contributes zero tools; that is
   734	        # an answer, not an absence.
   735	        # This daemon serves its whole surface as ONE page (each upstream is drained in
   736	        # Upstream.list_tools), so it never issues a nextCursor — and a cursor it never
   737	        # issued cannot be honoured. Refusing beats forwarding it into upstream cursor
   738	        # spaces it cannot belong to, which corrupted per-upstream pagination silently.
