{'experimental': {}, 'tools': {'listChanged': False}, 'extensions': {}}
This is a persistent proxy fronting MULTIPLE Xcode-adjacent MCP servers behind one endpoint: alpha, beta. Every tool is prefixed with its upstream's name (e.g. `alpha__SomeTool`) so two upstreams that happen to expose a same-named tool can't collide or shadow each other — always use the prefixed name shown in the tool list, never the bare upstream name.

If a call says 'not connected right now', that specific upstream is reconnecting on its own — the others are unaffected, since each upstream has its own independent connection. A short retry should work.

